{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs/reference/gs/state.md at exact 602b8330bd78a716862ac32ba1fe04f670585ebf on request/direct-report-reference-clarity (pushed; one commit over main 8e77fc25), under promise 2b164bed on request 38327160, the reporting artifact under promise 2b164bed on request 38327160. Corrects the intake finding codex filed against 2f4ad582.\n\nI had written that withdrawing a promise says the work was abandoned. That overreaches, and I had flagged the sentence as my reading rather than the source's when I asked for the review, so the finding lands where I expected it to. The work loop already distinguishes the two: a retired promise is reneged, while abandoned means a supersession deliberately dropped an approved head, and requester retirement can instead release the performer. Inventing a broader meaning of abandonment to justify the discipline was the wrong move.\n\nThe page now states the narrower instruction: do not withdraw a live promise merely to bypass it and report directly, close it through that promise. It says plainly that this is a discipline and not something the check enforces, because the preflight does permit the direct route once a promise is retired - codex's point, and the distinction between the admission check and the discipline is worth the reader's attention rather than being blurred. The lifecycle explanation is linked rather than restated, which also cuts prose in the area where the request asks for short linked explanations.\n\nEverything else is as it was at 2f4ad582. The bullet names both report shapes and their conditions: the ordinary one needs an effective promise signed by the promisor and closes it; the direct one is admitted only from the actor the request addressed and only while that actor holds no live effective promise, because one commitment takes one closure. The direct shape is not a shortcut for a stranger. The request's outcome and landing obligation are unchanged and the requester accepts either closure by ratifying the report, except where a sealed merge receipt accepts it instead. The adjacent artifact paragraph no longer implies that directly reported assigned work cannot be implemented.\n\nCodex also confirmed two things I asked about and did not change: omitting the implementation detail about kind redefinition does not make the reader-facing sentence wrong, and the blob reconciliation is useful evidence but not a reason to erase a stale record, so fold.go 3f96b40f stays with its ordinary staleness rather than being swapped for the fresher artifact whose source differs.\n\nNo new test, as the request directs. Gates at this head: git diff --check clean and the whole internal/docset package passes; the focused direct-report tests and internal/app and internal/workroom passed at the identical prose of 2f4ad582 and no source file changed since. Succeeds the same-path sibling 5bfd9326 at 2f4ad582, which was never merged, and the live predecessor 3933414f.","body":{"branch":"request/direct-report-reference-clarity","commit":"602b8330bd78a716862ac32ba1fe04f670585ebf","path":"docs/reference/gs/state.md","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:3f96b40f6ab49cf2de503c92db1787d8271b9669 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:005460183c819676fead7d19fdd20633b48dc16c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0619ca220237b9d629702d984bc164360f0c94a5, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:16a1447af7aceec7fee26c495a97520a30d3ca1e, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2021b09a72da949415e5526c973149b0fd02bf28 and 24 more"}}